<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Noman Celebicihan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1885">1885</a>–<a href="/years/1918">1918</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Noman Çelebicihan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Noman Celebicihan was a Crimean <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tatars">Tatar</a> lawyer, poet and the first elected mufti of the Muslims of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimea">Crimea</a>. In December 1917 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kurultai">Kurultai</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bakhchysarai">Bakhchysarai</a> proclaimed the Crimean People's Republic with him as its leader. When the Bolsheviks took Crimea in January 1918 he was arrested and shot in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sevastopol">Sevastopol</a>. He wrote the Crimean Tatar national anthem.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/noman-celebicihan.jpg" alt="Noman Celebicihan" width="320" height="448" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Noman_Chelebicihan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
